    description: "Found by the WI-lubap directed probe (2026-08-01, dev 529e4aebe3), which returned no_move.\n\nThe WI-lubap argparse join itself WORKS -- production _scan_argparse_commands resolves 26/26 of\nhypergumbo's own subcommands to 27 handler symbols against the real 41448-symbol survey. Yet the\nfull pipeline on this repo emits ZERO subprocess_calls edges (41448 nodes, 140086 edges, 90\nsubprocess_cli call-site symbols, 0 join edges). Three defects in\npackages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/subprocess_cli.py, the first two each\nsufficient on their own to force that zero.\n\nB1 -- CLI-NAME DETECTION IS ROOT-PYPROJECT-ONLY (:131-201 _detect_project_cli_name, guard :616).\nIt reads only <repo_root>/pyproject.toml, and only that file's [project] name and\n[project.scripts]. Any monorepo whose root pyproject is tool-config-only is dark by construction\n-- including this one, whose hypergumbo console script is declared in\npackages/hypergumbo/pyproject.toml while the root has no [project] table at all. It also never\nreads setup.py / setup.cfg entry_points.\n  Repro: _detect_project_cli_name(Path(\"/home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo\")) returns set().\n  Consequence: the guard \"if call.executable and call.executable in project_cli_names\" at :616\n  can never pass, for any call, in any such repo. Measured on this repo: 90 detected call sites,\n  0 executable matches.\n  Structural shape: walk pyproject.toml / setup.py / setup.cfg across the tree and union the\n  console-script names, rather than reading one file at one path.\n\nB2 -- ALL-OR-NOTHING ARGV PARSE (:98 ast.literal_eval, swallow at :127-128). The extractor\nliteral_evals the ENTIRE captured argv list, so a single non-literal element discards the whole\ncall site.\n  Real case: scripts/hypergumbo_diag.py:960\n    subprocess.run([\"hypergumbo\", \"slice\", \"--input\", in_path, \"--entry\", node_id_val,\n                    \"--max-hops\", str(max_hops), ...], capture_output=True, check=True)\n  raises ValueError, so _scan_python_file reports 0 calls for that file even though\n  SUBPROCESS_CALL_PATTERN matches at line 960. This is the single genuine self-invocation in the\n  repo and it is invisible.\n  Structural shape: parse element-wise -- walk the ast.List and take the leading run of\n  ast.Constant strings -- since the executable and subcommand are the leading literals and the\n  non-literals are always arguments after them.\n  Note the swallowing branch carries a \"# pragma: no cover\" pragma while demonstrably executing\n  on this project's own source; the pragma should come off once the path is covered.\n\nB3 -- HANDLER LOOKUP IS BARE-NAME, UNSCOPED (:410-412 index build, :440-442 lookup). LATENT: it\nproduces a confidently WRONG edge as soon as B1/B2 are fixed. _scan_argparse_commands indexes all\nsymbols by bare name with no kind or path filter, unlike _scan_fire_commands which enforces\nsame-file class scoping at :515-523 for exactly this reason. On this repo the subcommand \"survey\"\nresolves to two candidates -- the real cmd_run in cli.py and an external_symbol placeholder whose\npath slot is the external sentinel -- and the min-by-id tie-break at :627 selects the placeholder,\nbecause the sentinel path sorts lexicographically before the real one.\n  Structural shape: restrict candidates to the file the add_parser / set_defaults pair was found\n  in (mirror the fire scoping) and exclude external_symbol kinds.\n\nSEPARATELY, WORTH A DECISION RATHER THAN AUTOMATICALLY A FIX: the scanner is regex-over-raw-text\nwith no string-literal awareness, so a subprocess.run([...]) written INSIDE a Python string\nliteral is harvested as a real call site. The only two \"hypergumbo\" call sites the scanner sees\nin this repo are both fixture text inside test_subprocess_linker.py. That is why fixing B1 alone\nwould buy zero real edges here.\n\nVALIDATION AFTER THE FIX is the same directed probe, NOT a bakeoff slot: re-run\n\"hypergumbo survey /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo\" and assert at least one subprocess_calls edge\nfrom scripts/hypergumbo_diag.py:960 to cmd_slice carrying the subcommand in meta. Deliberately\nNOT tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: 501 repo roots under ALL_REPOS were scanned with the\nproduction functions and 0 have the joint construct, so no cohort can validate this either."  # 528e
