  message: "DONE via PR #154, merged to dev 226823c4c8.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (the item's own repro, re-run end to end on this repository -- the only\ninstrument that can see this defect; a cohort cannot, per the WI-lubap probe's 0-of-501 finding):\n\n  hypergumbo survey /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo --out <path>\n      --no-sketch-fan-out --no-handler-slices --no-progress\n\n  BEFORE (dev 529e4aebe3): 140086 edges, subprocess_calls = 0\n  AFTER  (with all three fixes): 140196 edges, subprocess_calls = 4\n\nThe four, each ground-truthed by opening the target source at the reported file:line:\n  scripts/hypergumbo_diag.py:960        -> cmd_slice            conf 0.85  GENUINE\n  scripts/dead-code-prospector-run.py:520 -> cmd_dead_code_maybe conf 0.85  GENUINE\n  packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_subprocess_linker.py:77  -> cmd_sketch conf 0.80  FIXTURE TEXT\n  packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_subprocess_linker.py:285 -> cmd_sketch conf 0.80  FIXTURE TEXT\n\nThe first is the join WI-lubap was filed for. The second is a second real self-invocation nobody\nhad noticed; both were B2 victims (each carries a variable in its argv). The last two are\nsubprocess.run([...]) written INSIDE Python string literals in the test fixture -- the scanner is\nregex-over-raw-text with no string-literal awareness. That is pre-existing and was not introduced\nhere; it only became visible because the executable guard finally passes. Filed separately rather\nthan folded in, because suppressing it means teaching the scanner about literals and that is a\ndecision, not a bug fix.\n\nA MEASUREMENT ERROR OF MINE, RECORDED because the correction matters more than the slip: my first\nreading of the post-fix artifact reported 0 edges and I briefly believed the fix had failed. The\nverification script filtered on a key named \"edge_type\"; the serialized field is \"type\". The\nfilter could never have matched, so it would have returned 0 for ANY input. Re-measured with the\nreal field: before 0, after 4. Note the BEFORE figure is unaffected -- it is genuinely 0, and the\nWI-lubap no_move verdict stands -- but it had been measured with the same unmatchable key by two\nindependent agents and by me, and was therefore RIGHT BY COINCIDENCE. Same shape as the WI-zulij\nfinding in the same session (an overlap ranked on a stored centrality field present on 0 nodes):\na filter naming a field that does not exist returns a clean, plausible, meaningless number. The\ntell in both cases is that the count is exactly zero on data that obviously contains something.\n\nWHAT THE UNIT SUITE COULD NOT DO. test_links_subprocess_to_argparse_handler has been green since\nthe WI-lubap fix merged in July while the feature was dead in production, because its fixture\ndefeats all three blockers by construction: a root pyproject WITH a [project] table (defeats B1),\na fully literal argv (defeats B2), and exactly one candidate symbol (defeats B3). Nobody chose\nthat; the smallest fixture that exercises a join is the one where nothing else is in the way.\nThis is the L13 masking pattern with the mask being a PASSING TEST rather than a missing one. The\nsix new tests are that same scenario with each convenience removed, so each blocker now has a\ntest that can actually fail.\n\nREGRESSION GUARD: the six red-first tests plus six pinning the fail-safe branches; subprocess_cli\nat 100%; 1841 tests pass across the 46 affected files; mypy ratchet delta +0."  # 5bd3
